      "condition": "MatchBox is a rust based implementation of BoxLang. My goal has been to keep MatchBox very clean and modular. I want it to be compatible with the BoxLang ecosystem but I want it to follow good software design principles and idiomatic Rust. I want to try and experimentally implement full compatibility with BoxLang on the JVM. Here is what I want you to do. - Review the BoxLang repo in ../BoxLang and transfer each and every test to MatchBox - Work through the test suite and get everything passing Constraints - EVERY BoxLang test should correspond 1-1 with a NEW test in MatchBox. - Do not ignore or skip a test in BoxLang core unless there is a hard requirement, document any skipped tests - Do not skip a test if there is already a test in MatchBox Do not use sub agents, do all the work yourself. Ask me any questions you need to get started or if something comes up.",
